# An end operation requires a mutable binding

Verifies an end operation through a const array binding is rejected, because
the operation mutates the binding it acts on.

>>> source
const values: int[] = [1]
values->push(2)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: cannot call `push` through immutable binding `values` at Span { start: 26, end: 32 }

<<< exit
1
